    /// Change counter of every shopping list
    ///
    /// One `{ list_id, version }` per list. The counter says *that* a list changed, never *what*: it moves whenever the list was renamed or its items were inserted, updated, moved or deleted by anyone - a household member, a meal-plan import, the CalDAV sync - and the row disappears with the list. Database triggers keep it, so no writer has to announce itself. A client polls this while a list is open and reloads a list through the same items request it used to open it; the write routes on items return `list_change: { list_id, before, after }` so the writer can tell its own change apart.
